Report #228: "Auto-Attune option is back, but I don't see a way
to filter the level of items you auto-attune"
(auto-attune options thread: toggle + quality filter + level
filter)

The option was not just missing a filter -- it was a lie. Since
2026-08-23 TryAutoAttune is an empty stub (auto-attuning was
retired because attuning CONSUMES the item, and auto-consuming
looted gear before the player could decide to wear it is hostile),
while the client's perk-gated toggle and the per-quality switches
kept storing auto_attune_on / auto_attune_off into
lg_account_meta that nothing read. The player unlocked the perk,
flipped the toggle on, and nothing happened except a switch that
said ON.

Change: the auto-attune path is revived behind real filters, so
the switch finally does what it says.

* Server (TryAutoAttune, on OnPlayerStoreNewItem): mirrors the
  retired body's safe parts -- the consumption is deferred one
  tick (m_Events + GUID re-resolve, so the item is not destroyed
  mid-add), the account row is read per item (auto_attune_on,
  auto_attune_off, auto_attune_ilvl), the per-quality opt-out
  mask still wins, and the new minimum item level must be met
  (proto->ItemLevel >= auto_attune_ilvl, 0 = no minimum). The
  actual attune goes through AttuneItemEntry exactly like
  ATTUNEALL, so a duplicate of an already-attuned entry is
  declined and SURVIVES in the bag (only first copies are ever
  consumed), followed by DestroyItem + RefreshStats + a chat
  line naming the item so nothing vanishes silently.
* Master switch defaults OFF: migration flips the column default
  to 0 and resets every existing account to 0 (rev_auto_attune_
  min_ilvl.sql in pending_db_characters) -- nobody's loot starts
  getting consumed because an old row defaulted to 1 while the
  stub made that harmless. Opting in is the toggle's job.
* New filter: AASET|lvl|<0-999> (HandleAutoAttuneSet) stores
  auto_attune_ilvl; the AA| addon sync line gains a 5th field
  carrying it (older clients ignore the extra field).
* Client: a Min ilvl button sits beside the Auto-Attune toggle on
  the items tab (StaticPopup numeric input, 0 = off), the AA|
  parser reads the new field, saved-vars defaults carry ilvl=0,
  and the Auto-Attune tooltip points at the new control.

Touches (module + one characters SQL): modules/mod-living-gear/
src/LivingGear.cpp (TryAutoAttune revival, HandleAutoAttuneSet,
SendAddonSync AA line), client_addon/LivingGear/LivingGear.lua
(button + popup + AA parse + defaults), data/sql/updates/
pending_db_characters/rev_auto_attune_min_ilvl.sql. No core
files.
